.IX Title "Lucy::Search::RangeQuery 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Search::RangeQuery 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Search::RangeQuery \- Match a range of values.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 10
\&    # Match all articles by "Foo" published since the year 2000.
\&    my $range_query = Lucy::Search::RangeQuery\->new(
\&        field         => \*(Aqpublication_date\*(Aq,
\&        lower_term    => \*(Aq2000\-01\-01\*(Aq,
\&        include_lower => 1,
\&    );
\&    my $author_query = Lucy::Search::TermQuery\->new(
\&        field => \*(Aqauthor_last_name\*(Aq,
\&        text  => \*(AqFoo\*(Aq,
\&    );
\&    my $and_query = Lucy::Search::ANDQuery\->new(
\&        children => [ $range_query, $author_query ],
\&    );
\&    my $hits = $searcher\->hits( query => $and_query );
\&    ...
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
RangeQuery matches documents where the value for a particular field falls
within a given range.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 7
\&    my $range_query = Lucy::Search::RangeQuery\->new(
\&        field         => \*(Aqproduct_number\*(Aq, # required
\&        lower_term    => \*(Aq003\*(Aq,            # see below
\&        upper_term    => \*(Aq060\*(Aq,            # see below
\&        include_lower => 0,                # default true
\&        include_upper => 0,                # default true
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Create a new RangeQuery.
.PP
Takes 5 parameters; \f(CW\*(C`field\*(C'\fR is required, as is at least one of either
\&\f(CW\*(C`lower_term\*(C'\fR or \f(CW\*(C`upper_term\*(C'\fR.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBfield\fR \- The name of a \f(CW\*(C`sortable\*(C'\fR field.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBlower_term\fR \- Lower delimiter.  If not supplied, all values
less than \f(CW\*(C`upper_term\*(C'\fR will pass.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBupper_term\fR \- Upper delimiter.  If not supplied, all values greater
than \f(CW\*(C`lower_term\*(C'\fR will pass.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBinclude_lower\fR \- Indicates whether docs which match
\&\f(CW\*(C`lower_term\*(C'\fR should be included in the results.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBinclude_upper\fR \- Indicates whether docs which match
\&\f(CW\*(C`upper_term\*(C'\fR should be included in the results.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS make_compiler
.IX Subsection "make_compiler"
.Vb 5
\&    my $compiler = $range_query\->make_compiler(
\&        searcher    => $searcher,     # required
\&        boost       => $boost,        # required
\&        subordinate => $subordinate,  # default: false
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Abstract factory method returning a Compiler derived from this Query.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBsearcher\fR \- A Searcher.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBboost\fR \- A scoring multiplier.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBsubordinate\fR \- Indicates whether the Query is a subquery (as
opposed to a top-level query).  If false, the implementation must
invoke \fBnormalize()\fR on the newly minted Compiler object before returning
it.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Search::RangeQuery isa Lucy::Search::Query isa Clownfish::Obj.
